# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only .cmd/.bat: it drops the
# first character of lines (`setlocal` reads as `etlocal`, `rem` stops commenting) and the
# script fails in confusing ways that look nothing like a line-ending problem. Every batch
# file in this repo was LF-only until 2026-09-03, which made `prose.cmd` unusable from
# PowerShell while still happening to work through Git Bash.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to *.ps1: PowerShell reads LF fine, so a rule there would
# renormalize every hook/tool script in the repo for no correctness gain.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
